  "problem": {
    "statement": "Version: deno --version\ndeno 2.7.7+e7eb863 (canary, release, x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu)\n\n\nit happens from time to time and its annoying when it happens because you might not notice you're running an old version of a pkg\n\nTo reproduce (not sure its 100% reproducible)\n- deno i -gfA npm:opencode-ai\n- deno run --allow-all --config /home/mrcool/.deno/bin/.opencode/deno.json npm:opencode-ai --version # works\n\nnow trying any other version , deno ignore it and jst use the cachezd one\n- deno run --allow-all --config /home/mrcool/.deno/bin/.opencode/deno.json npm:opencode-ai@1.3.5 --version\n- deno run --allow-all --config /home/mrcool/.deno/bin/.opencode/deno.json npm:opencode-ai@1.3.6 --version\n\nboth of these ignore the version i specified and use the cached version, if I remove --config part it works correctly\n\nthe config have this\n\n```\ncat /home/mrcool/.deno/bin/.opencode/deno.json\n{\n  \"workspace\": [],\n  \"nodeModulesDir\": \"manual\"\n}\n```",
    "source": "issue",
